<% content_for :title, "Home" %>

<%# Home dashboard, rebuilt on the ui primitives.

    Copy is sentence case throughout per design.md - the previous version used
    ALL CAPS for the h1 and Title Case On Every Word in the step copy.

    Airbnb/Stripe reading: one clear primary action, generous whitespace, and
    hairline borders rather than the heavy black outlines used before. %>
<div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl">

  <%= render layout: "components/ui/page_header",
             locals: { title: "Welcome to your financial journey",
                       description: "This is your launchpad to earn, invest, and grow." } do %>
    <% if current_user&.student? && current_user.portfolio %>
      <%= link_to "Go to the trading floor", stocks_path, class: "tw-btn-primary" %>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>

  <div class="space-y-6">

    <%# Funds available. The single number a student most wants, given the room
        to be read at a glance rather than buried in a pill. %>
    <% if current_user&.student? && current_user.portfolio %>
      <% balance = current_user.portfolio.cash_balance %>
      <%# .tw-card, not a gradient. This was bg-gradient-to-r from-sitf-hero-from to-sitf-hero-to -
          #f4d18d to #f8dba8, a tan-gold - and it was the only gradient in the app and the only use
          of those two tokens. Contrast was never the problem (slate-800 on it is 10:1); it was the
          one surface that belonged to no system. It also carried rounded-xl and shadow-xs where the
          panel tokens are rounded-2xl and shadow-sm.

          The piggy bank PNG is replaced by design.md's icon tile. Every finance app makes the
          numeral the hero on a plain surface - Robinhood, Monzo, Revolut, Fidelity, Vanguard, Cash
          App - and puts illustration in empty states and onboarding, not beside a live balance,
          where it competes with the figure and reads as marketing. The tile also fixes something the
          raster could not: the image was `hidden lg:block`, so on the phones most of these students
          use there was nothing there at all. %>
      <%# The tile sits on the label's line, not in a column beside the whole card. It used to be
          an items-start gutter, which indented the label, the figure and the supporting line
          alike - the balance, the one number a student is here to read, measured 77px from the
          card edge instead of 0. design.md had already ruled on this and measured it once, on the
          case-contact card. %>
      <section class="tw-card" aria-labelledby="funds-heading">
        <div class="p-5">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <%= render "components/ui/icon_tile", icon: "piggy-bank", tone: :success, sm: true %>
            <h2 id="funds-heading" class="text-sm font-medium text-slate-600">Earnings to invest</h2>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-2 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 tabular-nums">
            <%= number_to_currency(balance) %>
          </p>
          <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">
            <% if balance > 0 %>
              Ready when you are. Pick a company and buy your first shares.
            <% else %>
              You have no earnings to invest yet. Attendance and grades earn funds.
            <% end %>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>
    <% end %>

    <%# Announcements. The card is always padded now: the empty state is the compact
        variant, which carries no padding of its own.

        It used to render the full-height centred empty state - a 48px icon tile and py-12
        inside a card that already says "Announcements" and has three siblings. That is the
        page-level treatment, and it made a card with nothing to say the tallest thing on
        the screen. %>
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/card", locals: { title: "Announcements", icon: "megaphone", icon_tone: :info } do %>
      <% if @current_announcement %>
        <% cache @current_announcement do %>
          <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= @current_announcement.title %></h3>
          <div class="trix-content mt-2 max-h-120 overflow-y-auto text-sm text-slate-700">
            <%= @current_announcement.content %>
          </div>
        <% end %>
      <% else %>
        <%= render layout: "components/ui/empty_state",
                   locals: { compact: true,
                             icon: "megaphone",
                             title: "No announcements yet",
                             body: "When your teacher posts one, it will show up here." } do %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    <% end %>

    <%# Getting started %>
    <%= render layout: "components/ui/card",
               locals: { title: "Getting started",
                         icon: "compass",
                         subtitle: "Four steps from earning to tracking your progress." } do %>
      <% steps = [
           { title: "Earn funds", body: "Show up, stay engaged, and earn investment funds based on your attendance, participation, and performance." },
           { title: "Go to the trading floor", body: "Once you have funds, explore the trading floor and the companies you can buy shares in." },
           { title: "Buy and sell", body: "Choose your companies wisely. You can buy and sell as your portfolio grows, and watch your earnings change with the market." },
           { title: "Track your progress", body: "Your portfolio shows how your investments are performing over time, plus summaries of your grades and attendance." }
         ] %>
      <%# Four across at lg, one column below it. A 2x2 grid makes a numbered sequence ambiguous -
          1,2 reads across and 1,3 reads down, and nothing in the layout says which - so four
          short columns read left to right the way the numbers claim. This is the shape Stripe and
          Shopify use for "how it works"; neither draws connectors, which also avoids a decoration
          that only makes sense at one width.

          The numeral is a tile, not a filled circle. It was white on bg-sitf-primary at
          rounded-full: four saturated brand discs shouting over the copy they label, against
          design.md's rule that a tile carries the hue and a numeral is always slate-900. %>
      <ol class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 lg:grid-cols-4">
        <% steps.each_with_index do |step, i| %>
          <li class="flex gap-3 lg:flex-col lg:gap-2">
            <%= render "components/ui/icon_tile", label: i + 1, sm: true %>
            <div class="min-w-0">
              <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900"><%= step[:title] %></h3>
              <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600"><%= step[:body] %></p>
            </div>
          </li>
        <% end %>
      </ol>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</div>
